  "slug": "flow-matching-continuous-molecular-a38a",
  "summary": "Preprints on pretrained, in-context, flow and energy-score perturbation models arrive alongside benchmarks questioning single-cell foundation models.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is predicting single-cell transcriptional responses to genetic and chemical perturbations, with emphasis on generalizing to unmeasured conditions. The architectures differ. CytoWave uses two-stage perturbation-centric pretraining across datasets. RELAY conditions in context on measured control–perturbed pairs that share experimental context. GENESIS trains an energy-score generative model on covariates and approaches replicate-level reproducibility. SPEAR applies flow-based generation with spectral Laplacian gene encodings, and scDisentangle builds identity-preserving counterfactuals through sequential disentanglement. For compounds, GRAFT transfers genetic perturbation information to zero-shot drug-response prediction across cell types. UnDetect separates cellular context from compound effects using a multi-view kernel that includes Cell Painting morphology. ExPert inverts the task, inferring causal perturbations from observed states across 12 contexts. RAPTORGraph addresses causal discovery in Perturb-seq, and FateDriver prioritizes reprogramming regulators. Scrutiny accompanies new capability. Attribution analyses probe scGPT, Cell2Sentence and STATE, and a benchmark finds that five foundation models beat simple baselines only on specific tasks. A secondary strand covers spatial multi-omic integration and spatial protein inference.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-07"
}
